INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-an-c1','vce-bio34','written',183,8,NULL,'Explain why muscle cells short of oxygen convert pyruvate to lactate instead of simply stopping after glycolysis.','Converting pyruvate to lactate regenerates NAD⁺ from NADH. Glycolysis needs NAD⁺, so it can continue and keep producing 2 ATP per glucose.','Without NAD⁺ regeneration glycolysis would stop; the lactate step itself makes no ATP.',0,NULL,NULL,1,2,2.5,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ap-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',187,8,NULL,'Malaria parasites inside mature red blood cells cannot be detected by cytotoxic T cells mainly because:',NULL,'Cytotoxic T cells recognise antigen presented on MHC I, which nucleated cells display. Mature red blood cells lack nuclei and MHC I.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ar-c1','vce-bio34','written',194,8,NULL,'Explain how resistance to an antibiotic arises in a bacterial population, and why stopping a course early can make it worse.','Random mutations already give a few bacteria some resistance. The antibiotic kills susceptible bacteria, so resistant ones survive and reproduce, passing on the allele (natural selection). Stopping early leaves the more resistant survivors to multiply.','The antibiotic does not cause the mutation; it selects for it. Horizontal gene transfer (plasmids) can spread resistance too.',0,NULL,NULL,1,2,2.5,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-by-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',184,8,NULL,'Scientists are trying to engineer C4 traits into rice (a C3 plant). The main expected benefit in hot, dry conditions is:',NULL,'In heat, C3 plants close their stomata and rubisco binds O₂ more often. A C4 pathway concentrates CO₂ around rubisco.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-c4-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',181,8,NULL,'How do C4 and CAM plants reduce photorespiration?',NULL,'C4: CO₂ is fixed in mesophyll cells and released to rubisco in bundle-sheath cells. CAM: CO₂ is fixed at night (stomata open) and used in the Calvin cycle by day.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-1','vce-bio34','mcq',199,0,NULL,'A single-base deletion occurs in a gene. Where would it most likely have the greatest effect on the protein?',NULL,'A deletion shifts the reading frame for every codon after it, so an early deletion changes almost every amino acid. Introns are removed before translation.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-10','vce-bio34','written',199,9,NULL,'Design a controlled experiment to test how temperature affects the activity of the enzyme catalase. Identify the independent and dependent variables and two controlled variables.','IV: temperature (for example 10, 20, 30, 40, 50 °C, using water baths). DV: rate of O₂ production (volume of gas or foam height per minute). Controlled: catalase concentration and volume, H₂O₂ concentration and volume, pH. Repeat each trial at least three times.','A good design states measurable variables, a range of values, controls and repetition.',0,NULL,NULL,1,3,4.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-2','vce-bio34','written',199,1,NULL,'Explain how STR profiling and gel electrophoresis can show whether a man could be a child''s biological father.','STR regions are amplified by PCR and separated by size on a gel. A child inherits one allele at each STR locus from each parent, so every band in the child not from the mother must match a band of the biological father. One mismatch at several loci excludes him.','Mention PCR of STRs, separation by size, and the inheritance of one allele from each parent.',0,NULL,NULL,1,3,4.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-3','vce-bio34','mcq',199,2,NULL,'An inhibitor binds to an allosteric site on an enzyme. Increasing the substrate concentration will:',NULL,'Non-competitive inhibitors change the active site from elsewhere; more substrate cannot outcompete them.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-4','vce-bio34','mcq',199,3,NULL,'Light intensity is very low. Increasing the carbon dioxide concentration will most likely:',NULL,'The rate is limited by whichever factor is in shortest supply. With little light, few ATP and NADPH are available for the Calvin cycle.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-5','vce-bio34','mcq',199,4,NULL,'Mitochondria are isolated from cells and placed in a solution with glucose and oxygen. Almost no ATP is produced because:',NULL,'Mitochondria take up pyruvate, not glucose. Supplying pyruvate would allow ATP production.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-6','vce-bio34','mcq',199,5,NULL,'A patient receives monoclonal antibodies against a virus. This gives:',NULL,'The patient''s immune system did not make the antibodies, so no memory cells form.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-7','vce-bio34','mcq',199,6,NULL,'An mRNA vaccine cannot change a person''s DNA mainly because:',NULL,'The mRNA is translated by ribosomes into an antigen, then degraded; it does not enter the nucleus or become DNA.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-8','vce-bio34','mcq',199,7,NULL,'Influenza develops resistance to antivirals much faster than mammals evolve new traits. The main reasons are:',NULL,'Selection acts on variation each generation; many generations, many individuals and error-prone RNA replication mean resistant variants appear and spread quickly.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-challenge-9','vce-bio34','written',199,8,NULL,'Explain how one base substitution could have no effect, a small effect, or a large effect on a protein.','No effect: a silent mutation, because the genetic code is degenerate. Small effect: a missense mutation swaps one amino acid for a similar one or one away from the active site. Large effect: a nonsense mutation creates an early stop codon, or a missense change alters the active site.','Give a named mutation type and the reason for each outcome.',0,NULL,NULL,1,3,4.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-cm-c1','vce-bio34','written',189,8,NULL,'Explain how a cytotoxic T cell destroys a virus-infected cell, and why antibodies alone cannot clear an established viral infection.','The infected cell presents viral antigen on MHC I. A cytotoxic T cell with a complementary receptor binds it and releases perforin and granzymes, triggering apoptosis. Antibodies act only outside cells, and viruses replicating inside cells are hidden from them.','Mention MHC I, receptor specificity, apoptosis, and the location of the virus.',0,NULL,NULL,1,2,2.5,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-cr-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',174,8,NULL,'A gRNA is designed to be perfectly complementary to a 20-nucleotide target, but Cas9 does not cut. The most likely reason is that:',NULL,'Cas9 needs a short protospacer-adjacent motif (PAM, such as NGG) next to the target sequence before it will cut.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-cr2-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',182,8,NULL,'Cyanide blocks the electron transport chain. Which other stage of aerobic respiration stops soon after?',NULL,'The ETC unloads NADH and FADH₂. Without it, NAD⁺ and FAD run out and the Krebs cycle stops. Glycolysis can continue through fermentation.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-cx1','vce-bio34','multi',NULL,NULL,4,'Challenge: insulin from bacteria',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,11,14.0,NULL,'Original challenge question in the style of the VCE Biology exam, Section B','original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-cx2','vce-bio34','multi',NULL,NULL,5,'Challenge: responding to a new virus',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,1,12,15.0,NULL,'Original challenge question in the style of the VCE Biology exam, Section B','original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ec-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',178,8,NULL,'Which statement about NADP in photosynthesis is correct?',NULL,'Coenzymes cycle between loaded and unloaded forms, carrying electrons and protons from one stage to the next.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ed-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',191,8,NULL,'Some cancer cells display PD-L1, which binds PD-1 on T cells and switches them off. A monoclonal antibody against PD-1 helps treat cancer by:',NULL,'Checkpoint inhibitors release the brakes on the patient''s own T cells. This is immunotherapy, a form of passive treatment, not vaccination.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-edm-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',173,8,NULL,'A gene and a plasmid are both cut with two different restriction enzymes (EcoRI at one end, BamHI at the other). The main advantage is that:',NULL,'The two different sticky ends are not complementary to each other, which stops self-ligation and forces directional insertion. Ligase is still needed to seal the backbone.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-er-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',197,8,NULL,'Which pair of structures is evidence of divergent evolution from a common ancestor?',NULL,'Homologous structures share a bone pattern from a common ancestor but have different functions. The other pairs are analogous (convergent evolution).',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-fd-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',196,8,NULL,'Carbon-14 has a half-life of 5730 years. A bone has 12.5% of the ¹⁴C expected in living tissue. Its approximate age is:',NULL,'12.5% = (1/2)³, so three half-lives: 3 × 5730 = 17 190 years. Dinosaur fossils are far too old for ¹⁴C dating.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-fe-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',179,8,NULL,'Adding much more substrate restores the maximum reaction rate when an inhibitor is present. The inhibitor is most likely:',NULL,'Extra substrate out-competes a competitive inhibitor for the active site. A non-competitive inhibitor changes the active site''s shape, so more substrate cannot help.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-gmo-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',177,8,NULL,'Which statement about genetically modified and transgenic organisms is correct?',NULL,'A GMO has had its genome altered in any way (including editing its own genes); a transgenic organism contains DNA from a different species.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-gr-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',170,8,NULL,'A mutation in the trp operator stops the repressor from binding. When tryptophan levels in the cell are high:',NULL,'Tryptophan activates the repressor, but the repressor cannot bind the mutated operator, so RNA polymerase still transcribes trpE–trpA.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-he-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',198,8,NULL,'A fossil skull has its foramen magnum positioned centrally underneath. This suggests that the species:',NULL,'A central foramen magnum balances the skull on a vertical spine. In quadrupeds it is towards the back of the skull.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-hi-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',188,8,NULL,'A person has very few helper T cells (for example in advanced HIV infection). The most likely effect is:',NULL,'Helper T cells release cytokines that activate the selected B cells (clonal expansion into plasma and memory cells) and cytotoxic T cells.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ii-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',186,8,NULL,'Which sequence best describes inflammation after a splinter breaks the skin?',NULL,'Histamine causes vasodilation (redness, heat) and leaky capillaries (swelling), letting phagocytes and complement reach the site.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-mg-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',192,8,NULL,'Twenty birds colonise an island. One allele has a frequency of 0.6 on the island but 0.3 on the mainland. This is best explained by:',NULL,'A small founding group carries a non-representative sample of alleles by chance. Gene flow would make the frequencies more similar.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-nas-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',167,8,NULL,'A virus''s genome is analysed: 24% A, 31% U, 25% G and 20% C. The genome is most likely:',NULL,'Uracil means RNA. In a double strand, A would equal U and G would equal C; here they do not, so it is single-stranded.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ns-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',193,8,NULL,'Why are crops produced by intensive selective breeding often more vulnerable to new diseases?',NULL,'Low diversity means one pathogen can affect most of the population, as in the Irish potato famine.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-pb-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',185,8,NULL,'Prions differ from all other pathogens because they:',NULL,'Bacteria, fungi and protozoa are cellular; viruses contain nucleic acid; prions are protein only.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-pcr-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',175,8,NULL,'PCR starts with 3 copies of a target sequence. Assuming perfect doubling, how many copies are there after 10 cycles?',NULL,'Copies = starting number × 2ⁿ = 3 × 2¹⁰ = 3 × 1024 = 3072.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ph-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',180,8,NULL,'A plant is given water labelled with the oxygen isotope ¹⁸O. The label first appears in:',NULL,'Water is split in the light-dependent stage, and its oxygen atoms are released as O₂. The oxygen in glucose comes from CO₂.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-ps-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',171,8,NULL,'Humans have about 20 000 protein-coding genes but well over 100 000 different proteins. The best explanation is:',NULL,'Different combinations of exons can be joined from one gene, and proteins can be modified after translation, so the proteome is larger than the genome.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-psp-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',172,8,NULL,'Pancreatic cells are given a radioactive amino acid. In which order would radioactivity appear as an enzyme is made and exported?',NULL,'Secreted proteins are made by ribosomes on the rough ER, carried in vesicles to the Golgi to be modified and packaged, then exported by exocytosis.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-rp-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',176,8,NULL,'A plasmid carries an ampicillin-resistance gene, and its insertion site lies within the lacZ gene. Bacteria are grown on agar with ampicillin and X-gal. Colonies with the recombinant plasmid are:',NULL,'Only transformed bacteria grow on ampicillin. A working lacZ breaks down X-gal to give a blue colour; an insert in lacZ disrupts it, so recombinant colonies are white.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-sp-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',195,8,NULL,'Two frog populations can interbreed and produce fertile offspring in a laboratory but never do in the wild, because they breed at different times of year. This is:',NULL,'The biological species concept asks whether populations interbreed in nature. Different breeding seasons are a prezygotic barrier.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-tgc-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',169,8,NULL,'Methionine has one codon (AUG) and tryptophan has one codon (UGG). How many different mRNA sequences could code for the tripeptide Met–Trp–Met?',NULL,'Each amino acid here has only one codon, so only AUG UGG AUG works. For most amino acids degeneracy would allow several sequences.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-trp-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',168,8,NULL,'The template strand of a gene reads 3′-TAC GGA TTC-5′. The mRNA transcribed from it is:',NULL,'mRNA is complementary and antiparallel to the template strand, with U replacing T. Read 5′ to 3′: AUG CCU AAG.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-bio34-tv-c1','vce-bio34','mcq',190,8,NULL,'The herd immunity threshold is about 1 − 1/R₀. For measles, R₀ ≈ 15. Roughly what proportion of a population must be immune?',NULL,'1 − 1/15 ≈ 0.93. Highly infectious diseases need very high vaccination coverage.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
