INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-ed-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',230,8,NULL,'In a study of caffeine and reaction time, the caffeine group happened to include mostly experienced gamers. Gaming experience is best described as:',NULL,'An extraneous variable becomes confounding when it varies with the IV, so the results cannot be attributed to caffeine alone. Random allocation helps prevent this.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-ei-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',213,8,NULL,'Sara feels anxious every time she sits in a dentist''s waiting room, though she cannot recall any bad experience there. This anxiety is an example of:',NULL,'Classically conditioned responses are implicit: they are expressed without conscious recall of the learning event.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-ev-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',232,8,NULL,'A study uses only first-year university students, but its conclusions are applied to all adults. This mainly threatens the study''s:',NULL,'External validity is whether results can be generalised beyond the sample and setting. Internal validity is whether the study measured what it claimed.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-gas-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',204,8,NULL,'In Selye''s General Adaptation Syndrome, why is a person in the resistance stage more likely to catch a cold?',NULL,'Cortisol keeps resistance to the original stressor above normal, but prolonged release weakens immune function, making new illnesses more likely.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-gb-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',206,8,NULL,'Chronic stress changes a person''s gut microbiota, and the changed microbiota then worsens their mood. This best illustrates that the gut–brain axis is:',NULL,'The CNS and the enteric nervous system communicate both ways, including via the vagus nerve and chemicals produced by gut microbes.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-mn-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',217,8,NULL,'Why are Songlines an effective mnemonic for storing large amounts of knowledge in oral cultures?',NULL,'Songlines combine the advantages of the method of loci (place-based cues) with narrative, music and repetition.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-ms-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',218,8,NULL,'During REM sleep, the expected EEG, EOG and EMG recordings are:',NULL,'REM looks ''awake'' on the EEG, the eyes move rapidly, and skeletal muscles are nearly paralysed (atonia).',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-mw-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',225,8,NULL,'Which statement about the mental health continuum is correct?',NULL,'The continuum (mentally healthy, mental health problems, mental disorders) is fluid. Temporary, situational stress is usually a ''problem'', not a disorder.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-nr-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',219,8,NULL,'Across a typical night of adult sleep:',NULL,'Deep NREM sleep is concentrated in the first half of the night; REM periods lengthen in later cycles.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-nt-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',202,8,NULL,'A drug blocks GABA receptors on post-synaptic neurons. The most likely effect is:',NULL,'GABA is the main inhibitory neurotransmitter. Blocking its receptors removes the ''brake'', so neurons fire more readily.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-oc-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',209,8,NULL,'A car beeps until the driver fastens their seatbelt, and the driver now buckles up straight away. The behaviour has been strengthened by:',NULL,'Removing an unpleasant stimulus (the beeping) makes the behaviour more likely. Punishment always makes behaviour less likely.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-ol-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',210,8,NULL,'A child watches a cooking show closely, remembers every step and wants to cook, but cannot reach the bench or use the knife safely. Which stage of observational learning is not met?',NULL,'Reproduction requires the physical and mental ability to perform the behaviour. The child attended, retained and was motivated.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-pf-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',227,8,NULL,'Jake avoids every dog he sees, and his relief each time keeps his fear going. This perpetuation of the phobia is best explained by:',NULL,'Classical conditioning can precipitate a phobia; operant conditioning (negative reinforcement of avoidance) perpetuates it.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-pi-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',228,8,NULL,'Why are benzodiazepines not usually a long-term treatment for specific phobia?',NULL,'Benzodiazepines are GABA agonists that relieve symptoms short term. Systematic desensitisation and CBT target the conditioned response and thinking.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-pr-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',229,8,NULL,'Which set correctly matches a biological, a psychological and a social protective factor?',NULL,'Biological: adequate diet and sleep. Psychological: cognitive behavioural strategies, mindfulness. Social: support from family, friends and community.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-sd-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',222,8,NULL,'Research comparing sleep deprivation with alcohol suggests that being awake for about 17 hours affects performance roughly as much as a blood alcohol concentration of:',NULL,'About 17 hours awake ≈ BAC 0.05%; about 24 hours ≈ BAC 0.10%, above the legal driving limit.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-se-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',226,8,NULL,'Which is NOT one of the seven domains of social and emotional wellbeing (SEWB) for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples?',NULL,'The domains are connection to body; mind and emotions; family and kinship; community; culture; Country; and spirituality and ancestors.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-sh-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',224,8,NULL,'Using a bright phone screen in bed can delay sleep mainly because:',NULL,'Light, especially blue light, tells the SCN it is daytime. Mental stimulation from the content adds to the problem.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-sl-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',221,8,NULL,'Why do many adolescents struggle to fall asleep before about 11 pm?',NULL,'Adolescents experience a sleep–wake cycle shift of about 1–2 hours, while still needing 8–10 hours of sleep.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-sp-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',203,8,NULL,'A student practises violin every day for a year, then stops for several months. Which best describes the changes at the synapses involved?',NULL,'Repeated stimulation strengthens synaptic connections (LTP). With little use, connections weaken (LTD), which is why skills fade without practice.',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
INSERT INTO question VALUES('vce-psych34-tm-c1','vce-psych34','mcq',205,8,NULL,'Mia sees a new job as a chance to grow, although she knows it will be demanding. She then decides her friends and her mentor can help her manage it. Her two appraisals are:',NULL,'A challenge appraisal is stressful but focuses on potential gain. Secondary appraisal asks: what resources do I have to cope?',0,NULL,NULL,1,1,1.0,NULL,NULL,'original','unknown',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Imported from index.html (written for this site; some questions were drafted with AI help and then reviewed).','2026-11-18T08:22:45','2026-11-18T08:23:12');
